WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know our first guest
tonight from his work

00:00:01.468 --> 00:00:03.870
in such films as "The Hangover"
and "Crazy Rich Asians."

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:07.140
He stars in the new special
"Ken Jeong Cracks Christmas,"

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:10.810 align:start size:94% position:6%
which debuts on Buzzfeed's
YouTube channel December 12th.

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:11.778 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let's take a look.

00:00:11.778 --> 00:00:15.115 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Can I sit on your left knee?
-Sure.

00:00:15.115 --> 00:00:17.851
-I won't lie to you,
I haven't worked out in a while.

00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:18.752 line:92%
I don't want to hurt your knee.

00:00:18.752 --> 00:00:19.919 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, you'll be all right.
You'll be all right.

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:22.222 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I can plant my feet.
-You're all right, there.

00:00:22.222 --> 00:00:24.057 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're all right.
-Maybe just to --

00:00:24.057 --> 00:00:25.759 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, you've been pretty good,
huh?

00:00:25.759 --> 00:00:27.093 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Not really.
-Yeah, I know.

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:31.331 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is the happiest I've been
since "Crazy Rich Asians"

00:00:31.331 --> 00:00:32.932 line:92%
hit the top of the charts.

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:36.036
-Please welcome back to the
show, Ken Jeong, everybody.

00:00:36.036 --> 00:00:38.271 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:38.271 --> 00:00:48.281 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:52.318 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:00:52.318 --> 00:00:54.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Welcome back.
-Thank you.

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:55.555 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's wonderful
to have you here.

00:00:55.555 --> 00:00:58.491 size:88% position:44%
-Wonderful to be back.
-So, this -- you were --

00:00:58.491 --> 00:01:00.060 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was that a Santa School
you were at?

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:03.129 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. That was a Santa School
in Midland, Michigan.

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:07.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's 500
Santa Students learning, like,

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:12.005
in-depth character analysis
about being Santa Claus.

00:01:12.005 --> 00:01:13.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
No joke.
It's almost like --

00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:15.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
It is kind of like
watching Ed Norton

00:01:15.275 --> 00:01:17.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
dissect a character in a play
or something.

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:21.815
-And this is, I'm assuming,
to then be a Santa at a mall?

00:01:21.815 --> 00:01:22.382 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Santa -- Yes.

00:01:22.382 --> 00:01:27.020 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, these are at level 1,
mall-level Santas.

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:27.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Yeah.

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:29.122 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean,
I will say I'm happy to hear

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:31.324 size:88% position:44%
that level 1 mall Santas
take it that seriously.

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:35.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yeah,
it's like Meisner for Santas.

00:01:35.662 --> 00:01:38.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Gotcha. Was there anything
you learned there

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:41.801
that wouldn't be sort of what
you would expect to learn there?

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:45.872
-Yeah. They would go,
"Okay, I'm from the North Pole,"

00:01:45.872 --> 00:01:48.508
and the principal is like
"Where in the North Pole?"

00:01:48.508 --> 00:01:51.244 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, like, "I don't know.
A cul-de-sac or something?"

00:01:51.244 --> 00:01:52.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.011 --> 00:01:54.314 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, and then,
"Oh, you know, my wife..."

00:01:54.314 --> 00:01:55.515 align:start size:94% position:6%
"How long you been married
to Mrs. Claus?"

00:01:55.515 --> 00:01:58.284
I mean, all these little things
that none of these kids

00:01:58.284 --> 00:02:00.386 align:start size:94% position:6%
would ever give a crap about.
-Yeah.

00:02:00.386 --> 00:02:03.523
It seems that they think that
they're gonna be cross-examined

00:02:03.523 --> 00:02:06.893
when I feel like most kids want
to talk about themselves

00:02:06.893 --> 00:02:09.395
more than they want to find out
where Santa is from.

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:11.397
-They're like,
"Can you just give me the Xbox?"

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:12.398 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-You know, that kind of...

00:02:12.398 --> 00:02:13.833 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They're like, "Hey, Santa,
I didn't come here

00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:15.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
for your back story."
-Yeah, right.

00:02:15.969 --> 00:02:18.071 line:92%
"I'm not tiny Stanislavski."

00:02:18.071 --> 00:02:20.273 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But this entire special
is you going around

00:02:20.273 --> 00:02:23.843
and talking to different people
about holiday traditions.

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:24.744 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-Yeah. It's been great.

00:02:24.744 --> 00:02:26.179 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've never done anything
like that before,

00:02:26.179 --> 00:02:28.815 align:start size:94% position:6%
just kind of
going across the country.

00:02:28.815 --> 00:02:30.783 align:start size:94% position:6%
What I loved
about the Santa School,

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:33.186 size:84% position:42%
some of the backstories
are really incredible.

00:02:33.186 --> 00:02:36.756 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, you meet retired people
who maybe quit their job

00:02:36.756 --> 00:02:39.759
because of a health scare,
or maybe a heart attack,

00:02:39.759 --> 00:02:41.461 line:92%
and they have another calling.

00:02:41.461 --> 00:02:44.197
And I'm like, "So, when did you
choose to be Santa?"

00:02:44.197 --> 00:02:45.098 line:92%
And they take it that seriously.

00:02:45.098 --> 00:02:47.567 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I mean this
in a non-ironic way.

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:49.736 line:92%
It's like, "No, Santa chose me."

00:02:49.736 --> 00:02:51.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
They have that kind of --
It's so cute!

00:02:51.204 --> 00:02:53.873
-That's nice to hear.
-It's really nice to hear that.

00:02:53.873 --> 00:02:56.242 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, it was really --
-I mean, it's certainly nicer

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:58.278 align:start size:94% position:6%
than like, "I'm just in it
for the cash, man."

00:02:58.278 --> 00:02:59.412 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:59.412 --> 00:03:02.382
"Two words -- booze and chicks,
you know?"

00:03:02.382 --> 00:03:03.616 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.616 --> 00:03:05.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What percentage of them
have the real beard,

00:03:05.585 --> 00:03:08.354
and how many are fake beards?
Do you see a lot of real ones?

00:03:08.354 --> 00:03:10.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
-100%.
-100% were real?

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:10.990 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Real beards, yeah.

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:12.792 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is the Harvard
of Santa Schools.

00:03:12.792 --> 00:03:15.395 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, Harvard, yeah, yeah.
-That's great.

00:03:15.395 --> 00:03:16.129 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-It's pretty amazing.

00:03:16.129 --> 00:03:17.130 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You mentioned in the clip,
as well,

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:20.934
and I want to congratulate you,
"Crazy Rich Asians."

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:22.936 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:03:22.936 --> 00:03:25.772 line:92%
-I can only imagine how --

00:03:25.772 --> 00:03:26.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
It must have been
so exciting to film,

00:03:26.873 --> 00:03:29.576 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then the reaction to it
and the success of it

00:03:29.576 --> 00:03:31.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
must just be
an incredible post-script.

00:03:31.277 --> 00:03:34.347 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's the only movie
I've ever been a part of --

00:03:34.347 --> 00:03:36.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
Usually when you do
Hollywood studio movies, like,

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:39.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
"What's in it for me?
How do I get next level?"

00:03:39.052 --> 00:03:40.987 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this is the only movie
I've ever done

00:03:40.987 --> 00:03:45.925
where I'm happier for my cast
and my friends on the movie

00:03:45.925 --> 00:03:49.229
and also for the Asian-American
community, in general,

00:03:49.229 --> 00:03:50.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I have
so many friends --

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:52.732
Asian-American friends
way more talented than me

00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:54.133 align:start size:94% position:6%
who are filmmakers,
writers, directors.

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:57.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're getting their projects
green-lit in Hollywood

00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:59.239 size:84% position:42%
that have predominately
Asian-American casts,

00:03:59.239 --> 00:04:05.011
and now they're seeing that it's
financially feasible to do this.

00:04:05.011 --> 00:04:07.013 size:88% position:44%
I've never seen anything
like this in my career.

00:04:07.013 --> 00:04:09.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
And now that I have
two daughters, you know,

00:04:09.649 --> 00:04:12.385
11-year-old daughters and they
have these amazing role models

00:04:12.385 --> 00:04:15.722 align:start size:94% position:6%
like Awkwafina and Gemma Chan
and Constance Wu

00:04:15.722 --> 00:04:17.957 line:92%
and Michelle Yeoh, to me,

00:04:17.957 --> 00:04:20.693 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's been such a game-changer
for our community

00:04:20.693 --> 00:04:24.130
just because it actually
transcended our community.

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:25.365 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, congrats.
It really was something,

00:04:25.365 --> 00:04:26.599 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it was great to watch.
-Thank you so much.

00:04:26.599 --> 00:04:31.104
-And it was -- the film itself,
nominated for a Golden Globe,

00:04:31.104 --> 00:04:33.973 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then Constance Wu
nominated for a Golden Globe,

00:04:33.973 --> 00:04:34.674 line:92%
which is really exciting.

00:04:34.674 --> 00:04:38.411
-Yeah, never in a million years
we thought this would be

00:04:38.411 --> 00:04:40.747 align:start size:94% position:6%
up for Golden Globes
or Critics' Choice awards.

00:04:40.747 --> 00:04:43.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we're really
in the middle of it.

00:04:43.182 --> 00:04:44.183 size:81% position:41% line:92%
I just texted Jon Chu,

00:04:44.183 --> 00:04:46.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
the director
of "Crazy Rich Asians,"

00:04:46.119 --> 00:04:48.621 line:92%
and he literally said, "Insane."

00:04:48.621 --> 00:04:51.524
Like, that's all he was saying.
It's really nice.

00:04:51.524 --> 00:04:53.893 line:92%
-Another awards show right now,

00:04:53.893 --> 00:04:55.795 align:start size:94% position:6%
the Oscars,
they do not have a host.

00:04:55.795 --> 00:04:57.130 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know
if you've heard this.

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:59.699 align:start size:94% position:6%
There have been some articles
written that suggest

00:04:59.699 --> 00:05:00.667 align:start size:94% position:6%
one of the names
that have come up

00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:04.971
is a very funny person
who would maybe be a good fit...

00:05:04.971 --> 00:05:06.973 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hmm.
-is you, Ken.

00:05:06.973 --> 00:05:08.541 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mm.
Now, Ken...

00:05:08.541 --> 00:05:10.543 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:10.543 --> 00:05:13.746 align:start size:94% position:6%
...tell us.
Tell us.

00:05:13.746 --> 00:05:16.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Oh.

00:05:16.649 --> 00:05:17.850 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Looks ready.

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:21.187 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-He looks very ready.

00:05:21.187 --> 00:05:27.660 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was always taught
that when you set goals,

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:30.330 align:start size:94% position:6%
make sure you keep them
very high.

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:32.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-If I do not become

00:05:32.031 --> 00:05:35.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
the host of the Oscars, I will
consider not only my career

00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:38.271 align:start size:94% position:6%
but my life a failure.
-Yeah.

00:05:38.271 --> 00:05:40.807 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:40.807 --> 00:05:41.974 align:start size:94% position:6%
Any goal
that's out of your control...

00:05:41.974 --> 00:05:43.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, that's what you need
to marry yourself to.

00:05:43.676 --> 00:05:46.212
-...that doesn't really make
sense whether you do it or not.

00:05:46.212 --> 00:05:49.515 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-I want it so bad.

00:05:49.515 --> 00:05:50.817 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:50.817 --> 00:05:53.252 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Do you think?

00:05:53.252 --> 00:05:54.253 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:54.253 --> 00:05:57.056
There's always that risk.
-There's always that risk.

00:05:57.056 --> 00:05:58.758
-When you want something
that bad, you might come out --

00:05:58.758 --> 00:06:01.294
if you do it, you might come out
and look a little desperate,

00:06:01.294 --> 00:06:02.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then the audience
will get nervous.

00:06:02.595 --> 00:06:05.064 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Seth, my whole career
is desperate.

00:06:05.064 --> 00:06:08.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Seth, that is my brand.

00:06:08.601 --> 00:06:12.405 size:84% position:42%
I came out of the womb,
it was like, "Hello!"

00:06:12.405 --> 00:06:14.741 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

